course: dictionary
lesson: 8313
title: Robbers in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A robber is a person who steals from a person or a place, often using force or threats. The clues in a sentence can show you the meaning. «Bees turn flower nectar into honey to eat in winter, store it in six-sided wax cells and guard the door against robbers.» Guard means keep watch over, so the robbers must be creatures that want to steal the honey.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. "Guard the door against people who steal" still makes sense, so robber fits. Robber is a noun, and its plural is robbers.
explain: Robbers are often the villains in stories and games, like «cops and robbers». In the old days, highway robbers stopped coaches on the roads, and they were called highwaymen.
fact: A robber steals from a person or place, often using force or threats.
fact: «Robber» is a noun: one robber, many robbers.
fact: Robbers were a danger to the tombs of the pharaohs. Later pharaohs were buried in hidden rock-cut tombs in the Valley of the Kings, because robbers could easily find the pyramids.
fact: A highway robber, or highwayman, was an old-time robber who stopped coaches on the road.
fact: If a robber asks for your phone or bag, give it. Your safety matters more than things.
exercise: «Bees ... guard the door against robbers.» What is a robber in this sentence? | A flower that makes nectar | A kind of wax cell | *A thief that tries to steal the honey | A bee that keeps watch over the honey
exercise: «Later pharaohs were buried in hidden rock-cut tombs, because robbers could easily find the pyramids.» Why were the tombs hidden? | *To keep robbers from finding them | To make a game of cops and robbers | To keep the pharaohs warm in winter | To store honey for the bees
exercise: A robber stops you on the street and asks for your phone. What should you do? | Hide the phone behind your back and shout | *Give it to them, because your safety matters more than things | Argue with them and run away
test: Which word is the plural of robber? | robbing | robbery | robbed | *robbers
test: What did a highway robber do in the old days? | *Stopped coaches on the road | Guarded the bees | Sold honey by the road | Built pyramids
exam: Which sentence uses robber correctly? | Robber is the name of a flower | *The robber ran off with the bag, and the police chased him | The robber was a kind of wax cell | The robber made the honey in the hive
